§ `Sections 54E and 54F -- counterclaims beyond a court's limit`

-- src:1802 | 54E.—(1) Where, in any civil proceedings pending in a State
-- src:1803 | Court, any counterclaim or set-off and counterclaim of any defendant
-- src:1804 | involves a matter beyond the District Court limit, any party to the
-- src:1805 | proceedings may apply to the General Division of the High Court,
-- src:1806 | within such time as may be prescribed by Rules of Court, for an order
-- src:1807 | that the whole proceedings, or the proceedings on the counterclaim or
-- src:1812 | set-off and counterclaim, be transferred to the General Division of the
-- src:1813 | High Court.
@ref s 54E(1) (src:1802-1813)
GIVEN `the proceedings are civil proceedings pending in a State Court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the value in dollars of the matter that the counterclaim or set-off and counterclaim of a defendant involves` IS A NUMBER
      `the District Court limit in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the application is made within the time prescribed by Rules of Court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 54E(1) a party may apply to the General Division of the High Court for a transfer of the proceedings or of the counterclaim` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where, in any civil proceedings pending in a State Court, any counterclaim or set-off and counterclaim of any defendant involves a matter beyond the District Court limit, any party to the proceedings may apply" (a "where" that is not met answers JUST FALSE, ruling of 2026-11-05 (b))
        IF (NOT (`the proceedings are civil proceedings pending in a State Court`)) OR (`the value in dollars of the matter that the counterclaim or set-off and counterclaim of a defendant involves` AT MOST `the District Court limit in dollars`) THEN JUST FALSE
        IF `the application is made within the time prescribed by Rules of Court` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "within such time as may be prescribed by Rules of Court"; the time is in Rules of Court, which are not among the sources
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:1817 | (2) On any application under subsection (1) or on its own motion,
-- src:1818 | the General Division of the High Court may, as it thinks fit, and on
-- src:1819 | such terms as it sees fit, order —
-- src:1821 | (a) that the whole proceedings be transferred to the General
-- src:1822 | Division of the High Court;
-- src:1824 | (b) that the whole proceedings be tried in the State Courts; or
-- src:1826 | (c) that the proceedings on the counterclaim or set-off and
-- src:1827 | counterclaim be transferred to the General Division of the
-- src:1828 | High Court and that the proceedings on the claimant’s
-- src:1829 | claim and the defence thereto other than the set‑off (if any)
-- src:1830 | be tried in the State Courts.
@ref s 54E(2)(a) to (c) (src:1817-1830)
GIVEN `the order is made on an application under subsection (1) or on the General Division's own motion` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the General Division of the High Court thinks fit` IS A BOOLEAN
      order IS AN `Order on a counterclaim beyond the limit`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 54E(2) the General Division of the High Court may make the order` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "On any application under subsection (1) or on its own motion, the General Division of the High Court may" ("On" counts as "where", ruling of 2026-11-05 (c))
        IF NOT (`the order is made on an application under subsection (1) or on the General Division's own motion`) THEN JUST FALSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the subsection lists three orders and does not say "only"
        IF order EQUALS `Another order` THEN NOTHING
        IF `the General Division of the High Court thinks fit` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may, as it thinks fit"; the judgment is the General Division's
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:1836 | (3) Where an order is made under subsection (2)(c), and judgment
-- src:1837 | on the claim is given for the claimant, enforcement thereon, unless the
-- src:1838 | General Division of the High Court at any time otherwise orders, is to
-- src:1839 | be stayed until the proceedings transferred to the General Division of
-- src:1840 | the High Court have been concluded.
@ref s 54E(3) (src:1836-1840)
GIVEN `an order is made under subsection (2)(c)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `judgment on the claim is given for the claimant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the General Division of the High Court has otherwise ordered` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proceedings transferred to the General Division of the High Court have been concluded` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 54E(3) enforcement on the judgment on the claim is stayed` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where an order is made under subsection (2)(c), and judgment on the claim is given for the claimant, enforcement thereon ... is to be stayed" (a "where" that is not met answers JUST FALSE, ruling of 2026-11-05 (b))
        IF NOT (`an order is made under subsection (2)(c)` AND `judgment on the claim is given for the claimant`) THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the General Division of the High Court at any time otherwise orders" (a stay lifted by an "unless" answers JUST FALSE)
        IF `the General Division of the High Court has otherwise ordered` THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "until the proceedings transferred to the General Division of the High Court have been concluded" (an "until" bar ends when the event happens)
        IF `the proceedings transferred to the General Division of the High Court have been concluded` THEN JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:1846 | (4) Where no application is made under subsection (1) or where it is
-- src:1847 | ordered that the whole proceedings be tried in the State Courts, the
-- src:1848 | State Court has jurisdiction to try the proceedings, despite any other
