@ref s 54E(4) (src:1846-1849)
GIVEN `no application is made under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is ordered that the whole proceedings be tried in the State Courts` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 54E(4) the State Court has jurisdiction to try the proceedings despite any other provision of this Act` MEANS
    IF `no application is made under subsection (1)` OR `it is ordered that the whole proceedings be tried in the State Courts`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where no application is made under subsection (1) or where it is ordered that the whole proceedings be tried in the State Courts, the State Court has jurisdiction" (this subsection gives no jurisdiction on these facts; a "where" that is not met answers JUST FALSE, ruling of 2026-11-05 (b))
         JUST FALSE

