§ `Section 54G -- costs in cases transferred from one court to another`

-- src:1900 | 54G.—(1) Where proceedings are ordered to be transferred —
-- src:1902 | (a) from the General Division of the High Court to a State
-- src:1903 | Court;
-- src:1905 | (b) from a State Court to the General Division of the High
-- src:1906 | Court; or
-- src:1908 | (c) from one State Court to another,
-- src:1910 | the costs of the whole proceedings both before and after the transfer,
-- src:1911 | subject to any order made by the court which ordered the transfer, are
-- src:1916 | in the discretion of the court to which the proceedings are transferred,
-- src:1917 | and that court has power to make orders with respect thereto and as to
-- src:1918 | the scales on which the costs of the several parts of the proceedings
-- src:1919 | are to be paid.
@ref s 54G(1) (src:1900-1919)
GIVEN `the proceedings are ordered to be transferred from the General Division of the High Court to a State Court, from a State Court to the General Division, or from one State Court to another` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court which ordered the transfer has made an order about the costs` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 54G(1) the costs of the whole proceedings are in the discretion of the court to which the proceedings are transferred` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where proceedings are ordered to be transferred — (a) ...; (b) ...; or (c) from one State Court to another, the costs of the whole proceedings both before and after the transfer ... are in the discretion of the court to which the proceedings are transferred" (a "where" that is not met answers JUST FALSE, ruling of 2026-11-05 (b))
        IF NOT (`the proceedings are ordered to be transferred from the General Division of the High Court to a State Court, from a State Court to the General Division, or from one State Court to another`) THEN JUST FALSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "subject to any order made by the court which ordered the transfer"; what the order says is not among the facts the text gives
        IF `the court which ordered the transfer has made an order about the costs` THEN NOTHING
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

@ref s 54G(1) (src:1900-1919)
GIVEN `the proceedings are ordered to be transferred from the General Division of the High Court to a State Court, from a State Court to the General Division, or from one State Court to another` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 54G(1) the court to which the proceedings are transferred has power to make orders as to costs and the scales on which the costs of the several parts are to be paid` MEANS
    IF `the proceedings are ordered to be transferred from the General Division of the High Court to a State Court, from a State Court to the General Division, or from one State Court to another`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where proceedings are ordered to be transferred ... that court has power to make orders with respect thereto and as to the scales" (this subsection gives no such power on these facts; a "where" that is not met answers JUST FALSE, ruling of 2026-11-05 (b))
         JUST FALSE

